## std/compressus.d.pengu — raw declarations for the vendored `miniz`
## (`std_c/miniz.h` + `std_c/miniz.c`, public domain / Unlicense).
##
## This is the **internal** binding of `std/compressus.pengu`. Import the wrapper
## (`import std.compressus`), not this declaration file: the wrapper owns the
## `CompressionLevel` / `CompressionFormat` / `CompressError` model, the gzip
## framing that miniz does not implement, the file helpers, the hashes and every
## ownership rule.
##
## ## Why the header is `miniz_bind.h` and not `miniz.h`
##
## miniz is configured by macros that must be defined *before* it is
## preprocessed, and PenguScript has no preprocessor. `std_c/miniz_bind.h` is a
## four-line shim that selects the subset this binding uses
## (`MINIZ_NO_ZLIB_COMPATIBLE_NAMES`, `MINIZ_NO_ARCHIVE_APIS`, `MINIZ_NO_STDIO`,
## `MINIZ_NO_TIME`) and then includes the untouched upstream header. The same
## macro set is passed to `std_c/miniz.c` by `build_runtime.py` (`STD_C_DEFINES`),
## so the archive and every consumer bundle agree on one configuration.
##
## The shim is not cosmetic: under `-std=c99` GCC defines `__STRICT_ANSI__`,
## which makes miniz's `MZ_FORCEINLINE` expand to nothing and turns every
## `static` zlib-compatible alias (`crc32`, `inflate`, `zError`, ...) into an
## unused function that `-Wall -Wextra -Werror` rejects. See the comment at the
## top of `std_c/miniz_bind.h`.
##
## ## Why this file is hand-written
##
## `pengu bind std_c/miniz.h` does not digest the header: the preprocessed
## translation unit contains GCC 16's `typedef __typeof__(nullptr) nullptr_t`
## from `<stddef.h>`, which pycparser rejects. The 3.1.2 header is also a
## single-header library with dozens of `#define`s, function-like macros and
## struct-heavy `mz_zip_*` declarations that are out of scope here.
##
## The declarations below were transcribed by hand from the prototypes in
## `std_c/miniz.h`, following the type mapping `pengu bind` documents
## (`mz_ulong`/`unsigned long` -> `u64`, `size_t` -> `usize`, `unsigned char *`
## -> `ref to byte`). Only the surface `std.compressus` needs is exposed; the
## ZIP and PNG APIs are compiled out by `miniz_bind.h`.
##
## ## Regenerating
##
## ```text
## pengu bind std_c/miniz.h --output /tmp/miniz.d.pengu \
##     --include-paths std_c/ --system-includes
## ```
##
## The command is expected to fail on the `nullptr_t` typedef; a future pycparser
## release may fix it. When it starts working, diff the output against this file
## by hand and keep the documentation below.
##
## ## Smart linking
##
## `link "miniz"` is emitted only when this module is part of the compilation,
## and that is the whole contract. `build_runtime.py` archives
## `std_c/miniz.c` into `build/lib/libminiz.a`; a program that never imports
## `std.compressus` never receives `-lminiz` and never sees a miniz symbol.
## `tests/build/test_smart_linking.py` asserts that through `bundle.c`, the
## `--verbose` link line and `nm`.
##
## ## What miniz does *not* provide
##
## There is no gzip (RFC 1952) support: miniz emits and reads zlib (RFC 1950)
## and raw deflate (RFC 1951) only. `std/compressus.pengu` builds the 10-byte
## gzip header and the 8-byte CRC32/ISIZE trailer itself on top of the raw
## deflate stream. That framing is documented in `docs/COMPRESSUS.md` §"Gzip
## framing".
include "miniz_bind.h"

link "miniz"

# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Return status codes (`enum` in miniz.h)
# ------------------------------------------------------------------

## Success.
const MZ_OK as int is 0
## The end of the compressed stream was reached. Not an error.
const MZ_STREAM_END as int is 1
## A preset dictionary is required; miniz never emits it.
const MZ_NEED_DICT as int is 2
## An operating-system error (`errno`).
const MZ_ERRNO as int is -1
## The stream state is invalid.
const MZ_STREAM_ERROR as int is -2
## The compressed input is corrupt or truncated.
const MZ_DATA_ERROR as int is -3
## The allocator refused a request.
const MZ_MEM_ERROR as int is -4
## No progress is possible with the input or output space given.
const MZ_BUF_ERROR as int is -5
## The stream was created by an incompatible miniz version.
const MZ_VERSION_ERROR as int is -6
## A function argument is out of range (miniz-specific).
const MZ_PARAM_ERROR as int is -10000

# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Compression levels
# ------------------------------------------------------------------

## Store only: emits a valid deflate stream with no compression.
const MZ_NO_COMPRESSION as int is 0
## Fastest compression (`zlib -1`).
const MZ_BEST_SPEED as int is 1
## Best standard compression (`zlib -9`).
const MZ_BEST_COMPRESSION as int is 9
## miniz-specific level above `MZ_BEST_COMPRESSION`; slowest and not
## zlib-compatible as a *level*, but the emitted stream is still standard.
const MZ_UBER_COMPRESSION as int is 10
## Let miniz choose (`MZ_DEFAULT_LEVEL`, currently 6).
const MZ_DEFAULT_COMPRESSION as int is -1

# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Flush modes and window bits
# ------------------------------------------------------------------

## Accumulate output; return when the input is consumed or the output is full.
const MZ_NO_FLUSH as int is 0
## Finish the stream and emit the trailer.
const MZ_FINISH as int is 4
## Window bits for a zlib-wrapped stream. Negate it for raw deflate.
const MZ_DEFAULT_WINDOW_BITS as int is 15

# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# tdefl / tinfl flags
# ------------------------------------------------------------------

## Default number of dictionary probes used by `tdefl_create_comp_flags_from_zip_params`.
const TDEFL_DEFAULT_MAX_PROBES as int is 128
## Ask `tdefl` to emit a zlib header and an Adler-32 trailer.
const TDEFL_WRITE_ZLIB_HEADER as int is 4096
## Ask `tinfl` to parse a zlib header and verify the Adler-32 trailer.
const TINFL_FLAG_PARSE_ZLIB_HEADER as int is 1

# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# One-shot zlib API
# ------------------------------------------------------------------

## Returns the miniz version string (borrowed; do not `banish`).
declare mz_version into ref to frozen char

## Upper bound, in bytes, of the zlib output for `source_len` bytes of input.
declare mz_compressBound with source_len as u64 into u64

## Compresses `pSource` into `pDest` as a zlib stream at `level`.
##
## `pDest_len` is in/out: pass the capacity, read the produced length. Returns
## `MZ_OK` or a negative `MZ_*` status.
declare mz_compress2 with pDest as ref to byte, pDest_len as ref to u64, pSource as ref to frozen byte, source_len as u64, level as int into int

## Decompresses a zlib stream from `pSource` into `pDest`.
##
## `pDest_len` is in/out: pass the capacity, read the produced length.
declare mz_uncompress with pDest as ref to byte, pDest_len as ref to u64, pSource as ref to frozen byte, source_len as u64 into int

# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# One-shot raw deflate API (heap-allocating)
# ------------------------------------------------------------------

## Compresses a block to a `malloc`-owned raw deflate buffer.
##
## `pOut_len` receives the length. Release the result with `mz_free`, never with
## `banish` (it is not a `PenguString`).
declare tdefl_compress_mem_to_heap with pSrc_buf as ref to frozen void, src_buf_len as usize, pOut_len as ref to usize, flags as int into ref to byte

## Builds the `tdefl` flag word for `level`, `window_bits` and `strategy`.
##
## Pass `-MZ_DEFAULT_WINDOW_BITS` for raw deflate, `MZ_DEFAULT_WINDOW_BITS` for
## zlib.
declare tdefl_create_comp_flags_from_zip_params with level as int, window_bits as int, strategy as int into u32

## Decompresses a block to a `malloc`-owned buffer. Release it with `mz_free`.
declare tinfl_decompress_mem_to_heap with pSrc_buf as ref to frozen void, src_buf_len as usize, pOut_len as ref to usize, flags as int into ref to byte

# ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Checksums and allocation
# ------------------------------------------------------------------

## CRC-32 (ISO 3309 / ITU-T V.42) of `buf_len` bytes, continuing `crc`.
##
## Start a fresh checksum with `crc == 0`. This is the checksum gzip stores in
## its trailer.
declare mz_crc32 with crc as u64, ptr as ref to frozen byte, buf_len as usize into u64

## Adler-32 (RFC 1950) of `buf_len` bytes, continuing `adler`.
##
## Start a fresh checksum with `adler == 1`. This is the checksum zlib stores in
## its trailer.
declare mz_adler32 with adler as u64, ptr as ref to frozen byte, buf_len as usize into u64

## Releases a block returned by `tdefl_compress_mem_to_heap`,
## `tinfl_decompress_mem_to_heap` or any other miniz allocation.
declare mz_free with p as ref to void into void
